{"kind":"stack","id":"water-cycle-s1","title":"Evaporation, condensation and the water cycle","theme":{"background":"#eef6fb","foreground":"#1d3b4f","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Evaporation"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-d","content":"When liquid water is heated by the sun and turns into water vapour, a gas that rises into the air."}],"actions":[],"buttons":[{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Condensation"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-d","content":"When water vapour cools down and turns back into tiny drops of liquid water, forming clouds."}],"actions":[],"buttons":[{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What is the name of the process when water turns from a liquid into a gas?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Evaporation","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Condensation","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Freezing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Where does most of the water that evaporates come from?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Oceans, lakes and rivers","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Clouds","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Rocks under the ground","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"On which day would wet washing dry fastest outside?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"A hot, sunny, windy day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"A cold, cloudy, still day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"A cold, rainy day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"A puddle sits in the school yard after rain. The sun comes out. Do you wait and watch it, or do you go and get a towel?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Wait and watch","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Get a towel","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You watch closely. The puddle shrinks as the sun heats the water, which slowly rises into the air as vapour. Evaporation at work!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"You mop up the puddle quickly. Still, the water did not disappear: it evaporated into the air too, just faster with your towel's help."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Clouds form when water vapour does what?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Cools and condenses into tiny droplets","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Heats up and freezes solid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Turns into salt","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which of these would make water evaporate more quickly?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Raising the temperature","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Keeping it in a fridge","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Covering it with a lid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the water cycle quiz."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You now know how evaporation and condensation move water around our planet. Keep watching the sky and the puddles!"}],"actions":[]}}
